0015 — `--metrics-only`: a font atlas that measures and cannot draw.

`bake-font.ts` gains a mode that writes advances, kerning pairs, baseline
and line height exactly as the full bake does, and no coverage: every cell
is 1x1 (the core refuses 0x0) and empty, and byte 13 of the header carries
`FONT_FLAG_METRICS_ONLY` (bit 1, beside `FONT_FLAG_BOLD`). No outline is
read, so a 3,800-glyph charset bakes in the time the cmap takes rather than
the time its coverage takes. `tools/build.ts` exposes it as `--metrics-only`
and says so on the per-slot line.

Why: a measurement pass (pocket-motion `src/text/measure.ts`) reads widths
through the core's own `measureText` and never draws, but the bake it
measured against carried full coverage — 30.1 MB for one 72 px bold slot
over the level-1 GB2312 charset, so it had to be rebuilt per text instead
of cached per charset. With this flag the same slot is under 64 KB and the
pass is built once and booted per call.

The tofu advance is computed the same way in both modes and only its cell
is dropped, so the cmap differs from the full bake in exactly one byte per
entry: `xoff`, the ink's left-bearing shift, which a bake that read no
outline writes as 0 and nothing in measurement reads.

A host that renders must refuse a pak carrying this flag: it measures text
and draws none of it, which is a blank frame with nothing wrong in it.
pocket-motion's `hardenedBootWorld` does, unless the measurer asks.

By file:
- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`: `FONT_FLAG_METRICS_ONLY`; `gen-rust.ts` and
  `engine/core/src/spec.rs` (regenerated): `font_atlas::FLAG_METRICS_ONLY`.
  The core reads neither; the constant is published so a backend can.
- `framework/compiler/bake-font.ts`: `BakeOptions.metricsOnly`, a
  `metricsOnly` parameter on `bakeSlot`, `BakedAtlas.metricsOnly`.
- `tools/build.ts`: the flag.
- `tests/font-bake.test.ts`: the metrics-only bake against the full bake —
  bytes 10..12 equal, every cmap entry equal through the advance byte, kern
  section byte-identical and non-empty, the blob header + cmap + one byte
  per glyph + kern, and the full bake more than twenty times larger.

2026-10-22, rebased onto 66caf4e5: main's `bakeSlot` gained a
`fallbacks` parameter before this patch's `metricsOnly`, so the flag is the
eighth argument (`tests/font-bake.test.ts` passed `true` as the seventh
and would have been read as the fallback list). A metrics-only glyph from a
fallback face is keyed -1 for kerning, as 0009 keys a full one.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

